        "identifier": "https://github.com/scottnarmstrong/AVAnomalousDiffusion",
        "note": "The Lean formalization of Armstrong and Vicol, \"Anomalous diffusion by fractal homogenization\" (Annals of PDE 11 (2025), arXiv:2305.05048), required at commit d4dbc7b11fbf350667013d5ac98a3686f44093f5 (see lake-manifest.json). It supplies the ambient space and Sobolev notions (Vec, MemL2On, weak gradients, periodic H^1, taken there from the CoarseGraining formalization of Armstrong and Kuusi), the conventions for functions on the torus, stream functions and their flows, the existence and uniqueness of weak solutions, and parts of the analysis of that paper (flows and their derivatives, the Faà di Bruno formula, cell problems and correctors of the shear pulses, energy and Galerkin methods on the torus). Its velocity field fixes the parameter q in terms of alpha; the velocity field of the present paper, with q free, is constructed in this repository.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      }
    ],
